71
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:12,200
So unfortunately, we will not be able to fire it.

72
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:22,000
Another attempt to make a space-age gun was the Dardik.

73
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:27,500
What made the Dardik revolutionary was not so much the gun,

74
00:06:27,501 --> 00:06:28,720
but its ammunition.

75
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:32,960
Triangular plastic-coated bullets called trowns

76
00:06:32,961 --> 00:06:38,160
It was a revolver of sorts.

77
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:42,280
You took these little trowels and you put them in the magazine in the butt.

78
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:49,260
And as you pulled the trigger, it would kind of flop into the cylinder and you'd fire it.

79
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:51,040
And then the cylinder would rotate and it would fall out.

80
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:55,500
And it would pick up another one and then you'd fire it and then the next one would fall out.

81
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:58,080
The guns themselves were kind of flimsy.

82
00:06:59,380 --> 00:07:01,600
Nobody cared. What's the advantage to this thing?

83
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:09,960
Today, the Dardik is a collector's item, and its ammunition is so rare that a single trownd caused...

84
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:12,380
$50.

